# GLD-000 — Guild name

> **Summary:** Guild identity and operational profile.
> **Epistemic:** Who this guild is, its laws, and its operational context.
> **Pragmatic:** Full briefing for activating or coordinating with this guild.
> **Audience:** Agents

---

## Identity

The guild's name, motto, and the function it serves in the system.

## Operational profile

What this guild does, what authority it has, and what thresholds govern its
work. A guild is `governed` threshold (STD-001 §2): changing its charter
takes an ADR or an Oracle-approved PR.

## Membership

The agents that belong to this guild, and how membership is granted or
revoked. The roster is apparatus — a regenerable view of the `guild:` field
already on every agent (STD-001 §2, guilds/ note).

## Related

- Standards this guild enforces (`STD-NNN`).
- Missions that established it (`MIS-NNN`).
